From 165029eb2eb7d3b60900c5934f3c1d6788f971b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nabils <nabileo477@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:54:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add optional Metal spatial convolution for
 Richardson-Lucy deconvolution on macOS

Add a Metal compute backend for single-precision spatial convolution,
selected with the new meson option "metal" (auto, enabled, disabled;
default auto, only active on macOS). When enabled, img_t::conv2 calls
siril_metal_convolve_float for float images with an odd kernel size from
7 to 31 and at least 32 Mi kernel taps (pixels * kernel_size^2). Smaller
or unsupported inputs, and any Metal setup or execution failure, fall
back to the existing CPU implementation, which is unchanged. The FFT
branch of Richardson-Lucy is not affected.

The shader uses the same zero-boundary correlation and accumulation
order as the CPU code. The naive RL memory estimate in
deconvolution_compute_mem_limits reserves two extra float buffers when
Metal is compiled in.

Add src/tests/metal_convolution_test.cpp, covering the CPU/Metal
results, fallbacks, aliasing and concurrent calls. The test is registered only
when Metal is built, and skips when no Metal device is present.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
